        narrative: "Iceland is a unique geographic landform created by the intersection of the Mid-Atlantic Ridge (a divergent tectonic boundary) and a mantle plume (hotspot). This tectonic configuration forces the Eurasian and North American plates to pull apart, exposing the rift valley on land at Thingvellir. The rifting causes extreme volcanic and geothermal activity, with geysers, hot springs, and volcanic fissures shaping the basaltic landscape. Iceland utilizes this geological structure to generate 100% of its electricity and heating from renewable geothermal and hydro sources.",
