        did_you_know: "Lonar is one of only four known hyper-velocity impact craters in basaltic rock anywhere on Earth, making it a critical analogue for studying Martian geology.",
        why_it_matters: "Shows that cosmic events can leave geological signatures that continue to support unique, closed biological ecosystems for thousands of years. \n\n[Daily Reflection]: On this Day 101 of your journey, reflect on the structures of the past and how they shape your current choices."
